-- ADVERSARIAL PASS on batches 1-3 of energy-conservation-rest-points-seating.
-- Prompted by the owner: "adversarial pass. you should be reading your sources btw."
-- The four sources batch 3 admitted unread have now been read (abstracts + method sections via
-- PubMed). Every finding below is an error in MY work, not in the sources.

-- ============ A1. THE BATCH-2 OVERCLAIM (most serious) ============
-- Batch 2 prose asserted: "Six further sources were read ... Not one states a spacing figure."
-- FALSE as written. Only REF-00953 was read in full text (get_full_text_article) and REF-00954
-- was fetched. REF-00955..00959 were ABSTRACT-ONLY (get_article_metadata), as their own
-- verified_by_tool honestly records. An abstract that does not mention spacing does not
-- establish that the paper contains no spacing figure. The row-level metadata was accurate; the
-- PROSE built on it was not, and the prose is what a reader believes.
UPDATE evidence_sources SET
  verification_note = verification_note || ' || ADVERSARIAL CORRECTION 2026-07-26: batch-2 prose described this source as "read". It was NOT - only the PubMed abstract was retrieved. Any batch-2 statement about what this paper does or does not CONTAIN (specifically "states no spacing figure") is unverified for this row and must not be relied on until full text is obtained.',
  updated_at='2026-07-26', updated_by_session='session_2026-07-26-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-adversarial'
WHERE ref_id IN ('REF-00955','REF-00956','REF-00957','REF-00958','REF-00959');

-- ============ A2. SAME DATASET ADMITTED TWICE ============
-- REF-00963 (IJOSE 2001, 7(1):15-34) and REF-00964 (Appl Ergon 2000, 31(3):329-32) are the SAME
-- STUDY: both n=171 elderly people aged 65+, both metropolitan Sydney NSW, both Kothiyal &
-- Tettey. The 2000 paper is a 4-page data note (22 body dimensions); the 2001 paper is the
-- 20-page treatment adding design implications and application examples. Batch 3 admitted them
-- as two rows without noting this, inflating the apparent source count. This is the SAME ERROR
-- CLASS I caught in batch 1 when Wheels for Wellbeing's 50m turned out to cite the DfT standard
-- it appeared to corroborate - committed by me this time.
UPDATE evidence_sources SET
  notes = notes || ' || ADVERSARIAL CORRECTION 2026-07-26 - NOT AN INDEPENDENT SOURCE FROM REF-00964. Abstract now read: "In all 171 elderly people (males and females, aged 65 years and above) took part in the study", metropolitan Sydney NSW. REF-00964 reports THE SAME 171-person Sydney dataset. These two rows are companion reports of ONE study, not two sources, and must never be counted as independent corroboration of each other. This is the same double-count error class the batch-1 adversarial check caught on the 50m interval.',
  updated_at='2026-07-26', updated_by_session='session_2026-07-26-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-adversarial'
WHERE ref_id='REF-00963';

UPDATE evidence_sources SET
  notes = notes || ' || ADVERSARIAL CORRECTION 2026-07-26 - NOT AN INDEPENDENT SOURCE FROM REF-00963. Abstract now read: "An anthropometric data set on 171 elderly people in Australia ... 22 body dimensions ... metropolitan Sydney, New South Wales". Same study as REF-00963, published as a short data note in Applied Ergonomics 31(3):329-32 alongside the fuller IJOSE 7(1):15-34 treatment. Companion reports of ONE dataset. My batch-3 note calling this "probably the underlying dataset" for REF-00963 was half right - it is the same data, not an upstream source.',
  updated_at='2026-07-26', updated_by_session='session_2026-07-26-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-adversarial'
